**=================================================================================================
** BONDED ANCHOR PRY-OUT  --  explicit dynamic (NEDParallel), Gauss-point-to-segment contact
**=================================================================================================
** One of four variants of the same model. See README.md for what the example is and how to run it.
**
**     pryout_implicit_nts.inp    implicit static  + node-to-surface contact
**     pryout_implicit_gpts.inp   implicit static  + Gauss-point-to-segment contact
**     pryout_explicit_nts.inp    explicit dynamic + node-to-surface contact
**     pryout_explicit_gpts.inp   explicit dynamic + Gauss-point-to-segment contact
**
** Everything the four have in common lives in the shared includes below, so a variant is only the
** four lines that make it that variant. All four ramp the fixture plate to the SAME 1.5 mm, so they
** are comparable at equal load rather than at equal time.
**
**   edelweissfe pryout_explicit_gpts.inp
**
** and then, once all four have run:
**
**   python plot_damage_comparison.py
**=================================================================================================
*include, input=./materials_explicit.inc
*include, input=./model.inc
*include, input=./contact_gpts.inc
*include, input=./adaptivity.inc
*include, input=./outputs.inc
*include, input=./steps_explicit.inc

*job, name=pryOut, domain=3d
